<title>CHINA: China 1996 sugar imports slump 57.5 pct.</title>
<headline>China 1996 sugar imports slump 57.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>China's sugar imports totalled 1.25 million tonnes in 1996, down 57.5 percent from 1995, customs figures showed on Thursday.</p>
<p>China imported 90,000 tonnes of sugar in December alone.</p>
<p>China imported 2.95 million tonnes of sugar in 1995.</p>
<p>Exports reached 664,783 tonnes in 1996, up by 38.3 percent compared with a year ago, the figures showed.</p>
<p>China exported 48,244 tonnes of sugar in December alone.</p>
<p>Exports totalled 480,425 tonnes in 1995.</p>
</text>
